00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.740
Microsoft's Linux story
goes back further

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.630
than most people realize.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:58.410
In 2009, we released
20,000 lines of code

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:03.840
into the Linux kernel, and yes,
the headline was "Pigs do fly."

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.160
By 2011, Microsoft was one
of the top five contributors

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.220
to the Linux kernel,
driven by our investment

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.980
in Hyper-V and virtualization.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.800
In 2015, we released VS Code

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.590
and co-founded the
Node.js Foundation.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.560
By 2018, we'd acquired GitHub,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.560
VS Code was the number
one developer tool,

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.400
and Azure was trending
towards 50% Linux workloads.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.920
Then in 2019, we shipped
the Linux kernel for WSL,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.700
and we quietly released an
internal project called

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.160
